==English==

===Etymology===
{{compound|there|about|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# near that [[place]], [[time]] or [[date]]
#: ''Dinner will be ready at 6:30 or '''thereabout'''.''
# approximately that [[number]]
#: ''The speed of light is 185,000 miles per hour, right? - Yes, '''thereabout'''.''
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} concerning that; about that
#: ''What will ye dine? I will go '''thereabout'''.'' &mdash; Chaucer.
#: ''They were much perplexed '''thereabout'''.'' &mdash; Luke xxiv. 4.

